WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:02.680
&lt;i&gt;Election meddling&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:02.680 --> 00:00:06.200
&lt;i&gt;Fellas, I need 11,000 votes give me a break&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:08.600
&lt;i&gt;The mishandling of classified documents...&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:11.560
&lt;i&gt;It’s an unprecedented day in American history&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:14.800
...and the falsifying of business records

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:18.680
&lt;i&gt;Alvin Bragg is investigating former president Trump regarding a hush money payment&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:23.760
Just some of the 91 criminal charges facing Donald Trump

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:28.800
&lt;i&gt;I am a victim of one of the great political smear campaigns...&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:30.360
&lt;i&gt;...in the history of our country&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:33.200
&lt;i&gt;But how much jeopardy is he really in?&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:41.560
Across four criminal cases...

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:49.400
...Trump faces 44 federal and 47 state charges, all of them felonies

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:54.840
First up, Trump will face independent special prosecutor Jack Smith’s indictment

00:00:54.840 --> 00:01:00.000
&lt;i&gt;The attack on our nation’s Capitol on January 6th 2021...&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.080
&lt;i&gt;...was an unprecedented assault on the seat of American democracy&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:06.920
Courts will consider four charges...

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:10.680
...including conspiracy to defraud the United States

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:16.320
The indictment alleges Trump set out to sabotage the constitutional process...

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:20.160
...by manipulating the election in several states

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:23.840
&lt;i&gt;You don’t concede when there’s theft involved&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:29.600
And exploiting violence at the Capitol to delay certification of the vote

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:38.120
That same month, Manhattan’s top prosecutor Alvin Bragg...

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:40.040
...begins a separate trial

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:46.040
Trump is charged with 34 counts of falsifying business records...

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:50.120
&lt;i&gt;Donald Trump has become the first former United States president...&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:51.400
&lt;i&gt;...to face criminal charges&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:56.360
...in order to cover up an alleged $130,000...

00:01:56.360 --> 00:01:59.440
...hush money payment to porn star Stormy Daniels

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:06.160
Next up, Mr Smith will be back to bring a separate case

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:10.920
Alleging Trump kept secret documents long after he left the White House

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:17.520
He’ll face 40 charges, including 31 counts of violations of the Espionage Act...

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:20.040
...of 1917

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:23.400
&lt;i&gt;They alleged Trump stored boxes with classified documents...&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:25.160
&lt;i&gt;...all over the place in Mar a Lago, frankly...&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:29.760
...including some detailing America’s nuclear secrets

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:36.360
Finally, Trump will face prosecutor Fani Willis in court...

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:39.120
...but his trial date hasn’t been set yet

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:45.160
The court will consider 13 charges, including racketeering...

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:48.280
...a law originally designed to target the Mafia

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:52.680
The statute ties 19 co-defendants together...

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:56.560
&lt;i&gt;The grand jury believes they were part of the illegal effort...&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:56.560 --> 00:03:01.800
&lt;i&gt;...to overturn the result of Georgia’s 2020 presidential election&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:06.880
...and alleges Trump was the boss of this criminal enterprise

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:09.040
Central to the case will be Trump’s...

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:13.080
...alleged attempt to put pressure on Georgia’s secretary of state...

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:16.960
...to find the exact number of votes needed to win

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:29.160
Four of Trump’s co-defendants have now taken plea deals...

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:32.080
...so the evidence is mounting against him

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:36.960
All this before even mentioning two ongoing civil trials in New York

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:42.640
But what will this litany of allegations do to his political campaign?

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:49.760
The clashes between Trump’s campaign diary and his court appearances...

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:52.120
...like the one on January 15th...

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:57.520
...where Trump is due at a Republican caucus and a civil trial simultaneously...

00:03:57.520 --> 00:04:03.000
...may turn the 2024 election into a crusade to keep him out of prison

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:06.960
But even if Trump is found guilty, it’s unlikely he would see...

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:10.000
...the inside of a prison cell before the election

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:14.120
&lt;i&gt;When you go to bed at night, do you worry about going to jail?&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:16.200
&lt;i&gt;No, I don’t, really&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:20.600
Legal appeals are unlikely to conclude by November...

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:24.000
...and if he takes the White House for a second term...

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:27.000
...Trump could even attempt to pardon himself

00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:30.680
&lt;i&gt;This trial is a total witch hunt&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:35.760
Incredibly even if Trump is convicted before the election...

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:40.680
...there is nothing preventing him running for office from behind bars

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:46.080
By posing as a victim of political persecution...

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:50.360
...Trump has made his campaign about the cases against him...

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:53.640
...leveraging the trials to galvanise his base...

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:57.320
...which increases pressure on his own party to back him

00:04:57.320 --> 00:05:01.200
&lt;i&gt;If former President Trump is convicted in a court of law...&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:04.480
&lt;i&gt;...would you still support him as your party’s choice?&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:07.360
&lt;i&gt;Please raise your hand if you would&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:12.680 --> 00:05:13.840
It’s working

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:18.360
Trump is likely to be the next Republican nominee, and his polling...

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:21.120
...only improved as the indictments were filed

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:26.240
&lt;i&gt;Trump now has the biggest lead over his 2024 Republican challengers&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:29.560
Whatever happens in Trump’s court cases...

00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:32.920
...it’s clear he will play the outcome to his political advantage

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:39.800
Far from damaging his campaign, Trump’s legal storms are helping it

